WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.032 --> 00:00:05.555
Journal Entry: March 17, 1875, Transylvania My name is Jonathan Harker and I work as a realtor for a

2
00:00:05.556 --> 00:00:15.523
London office, negotiating deals for foreign clients who wish to purchase an English residence or business. My position

3
00:00:15.524 --> 00:00:24.531
requires me to scout out a suitable property to match each client's interests and prepare the legal paperwork for

4
00:00:24.532 --> 00:00:34.436
the transaction. One day, my employer received correspondence from Count Dracula in the country of Transylvania, located beside

5
00:00:34.437 --> 00:00:42.182
Russia on the coast of the Black Sea. He was interested in immigrating to England and wanted us to

6
00:00:42.183 --> 00:00:51.658
find him a home that would satisfy a particular set of conditions. It took me almost three weeks to

7
00:00:51.659 --> 00:00:59.933
secure a property that he found acceptable, but after he reviewed the property, I managed to settle on

8
00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:06.155
a good price. Then, much to my chagrin, he requested that I deliver the paperwork to him personally at

9
00:01:06.156 --> 00:01:15.085
his castle in Transylvania. I discussed the situation with my fiancée, Mina, and she encouraged me to make the

10
00:01:15.086 --> 00:01:20.996
trip. We were planning to be married in the autumn and the trip would possibly postpone our plans,

11
00:01:20.997 --> 00:01:28.274
but I knew that the count's business was important. I did not know then that I would be placing

12
00:01:28.275 --> 00:01:36.488
myself and my beautiful Mina in terrible danger. It was a long and difficult journey to Transylvania, first

13
00:01:36.489 --> 00:01:45.369
by boat from England and then on land by coach. Finally, after several days of travel, we reached a

14
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:55.012
small town called Bistritz, nestled at the foot of a high mountain ridge. The driver informed me that his

15
00:01:55.013 --> 00:01:57.777
horses needed to be fed and rested, so I stepped out of the coach and found a quaint

16
00:01:57.778 --> 00:02:02.336
little inn where I could eat supper. The atmosphere was warm and friendly, and before too long, I was

17
00:02:02.337 --> 00:02:08.415
approached by the kind innkeeper, who offered me a glass of ale and a mutton steak. "Where are

18
00:02:08.416 --> 00:02:13.963
you headed?" he asked. "I'm taking some legal papers to Castle Dracula," I replied. A sudden hush came over

19
00:02:13.964 --> 00:02:22.820
the room; everyone stopped what they were doing and turned to look at me. "Here," said the innkeeper, taking

20
00:02:22.821 --> 00:02:29.360
a gold cross from his neck and handing it to me. "You shouldn't go there. But if you

21
00:02:29.361 --> 00:02:35.200
must, take this. It can't completely protect you, but at least it's something." I hesitantly put it on, and

22
00:02:35.201 --> 00:02:42.461
as I turned to leave, I thought I heard someone say "vampire." The winding road up to Castle Dracula

23
00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:48.001
was rugged, yet we were driving at a modest pace. The air had turned frigid once the sun

24
00:02:48.002 --> 00:02:54.779
set behind the mountains, and for the first time, I realized just how high we'd climbed. I felt chilled

25
00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.136
from the inside out, as though someone had sucked all the heat from my body. I buttoned up

26
00:02:59.137 --> 00:03:02.874
my coat and sank down into my seat, hoping to stay warm, but it was no use. I stared

27
00:03:02.875 --> 00:03:12.564
up at the dark, foreboding sky and thought of Mina. Finally, just after three o'clock, we arrived at the

28
00:03:12.565 --> 00:03:16.469
castle. I quickly climbed out of the coach, and had barely enough time to retrieve my suitcase before

29
00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:22.040
the driver cracked his whip and his horses sped off into the darkness. "Good evening, sir," a voice spoke

30
00:03:22.041 --> 00:03:28.469
from behind me. Startled, I turned around and saw that there was a queer-looking man standing in the

31
00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:32.135
doorway. He had white hair, was unnaturally tall, and wore a suit that was completely black. "I am Count

32
00:03:32.136 --> 00:03:40.508
Dracula. Please, follow me." I picked up my suitcase and followed the count through the castle's massive wooden doors,

33
00:03:40.509 --> 00:03:50.238
which he locked behind us, and up a flight of stairs. We came to a large, open living

34
00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:53.565
room, and I was pleased to find food and wine set out for me on a small table in

35
00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:59.701
front of a warm fireplace. "Your room is down the hall," he explained. After I had put my suitcase

36
00:03:59.702 --> 00:04:07.168
away and freshened up, we sat down together at the table by the fire. The count did not

37
00:04:07.169 --> 00:04:16.486
eat; he patiently watched me finish my meal, and then talked briefly about the history of the castle. As

38
00:04:16.487 --> 00:04:21.891
he was speaking, I couldn't help noticing that his hands were covered in fine hair, like animal fur,

39
00:04:21.892 --> 00:04:29.081
and that his fingers were long and bony. The next morning I awoke with a start, quickly washed, and

40
00:04:29.082 --> 00:04:34.994
changed into my suit. Then I went downstairs to find my host and discovered that there was no one

41
00:04:34.995 --> 00:04:40.208
to be found in the castle─not even a servant! There was only a note that read: Mr. Harker,

42
00:04:40.209 --> 00:04:44.590
Please feel free to explore the castle. But, if you come to a locked room, please do not attempt

43
00:04:44.591 --> 00:04:53.598
to enter it. Enjoy your breakfast. We shall discuss more tonight. I wandered back up the stairs and noticed

44
00:04:53.599 --> 00:05:00.725
that a simple breakfast of bread, ham, and water had been set out for me by the fire.

45
00:05:00.726 --> 00:05:09.836
After eating, I returned to my room rather unsatisfied and applied myself to preparing the final paperwork. I hoped

46
00:05:09.837 --> 00:05:15.693
that we would be able to finalize the purchase that night and I could begin the long journey

47
00:05:15.694 --> 00:05:22.907
home the next day. I was sorely mistaken. I was preparing for bed that evening when the count knocked

48
00:05:22.908 --> 00:05:31.709
on my door and called me into the living room. We sat by the fire, and he asked me

49
00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:35.351
a series of seemingly bizarre questions about the home I had selected for him. I explained to him

50
00:05:35.352 --> 00:05:41.235
that it was a large, secluded property fenced in by a tall stone wall and surrounded by plenty of

51
00:05:41.236 --> 00:05:45.937
old trees. "It even has its own parish chapel," I told him. "Ah! Does it have a cemetery

52
00:05:45.938 --> 00:05:49.056
too? So I would be close to the dead?" he asked. I was thrown by his question─why would he

53
00:05:49.057 --> 00:05:56.070
care about such things? What could he possibly want with a cemetery? We continued talking for a long time,

54
00:05:56.071 --> 00:06:00.965
and I became so tired that I began to drift off. All of a sudden, I jerked awake

55
00:06:00.966 --> 00:06:07.314
and found the count's face close to mine. I could smell his foul breath─like the smell of death─and almost

56
00:06:07.315 --> 00:06:10.457
gagged in disgust. I apologized and retired to my room. The next evening, I was relieved to discover that

57
00:06:10.458 --> 00:06:17.862
the count had signed the paperwork, but my happiness was quickly quashed. He asked me if I would

58
00:06:17.863 --> 00:06:27.933
be able to stay on in Transylvania for another month to assist him with some logistical concerns about transporting

59
00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:34.933
his material goods to England. I was disappointed; however, I reluctantly agreed because I felt I had no

60
00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:44.735
choice. For the next fortnight, we met regularly, always after sunset, to discuss English culture, politics, and what he

61
00:06:44.736 --> 00:06:52.584
should expect in his new environment. In addition, I helped him arrange cargo shipping by boat, although he admitted

62
00:06:52.585 --> 00:07:00.394
that he had few material goods to transport. All the talk of the sea reminded me that Mina

63
00:07:00.395 --> 00:07:04.818
was scheduled to visit her best friend, Lucy, at her seaside home this summer. I foolishly told the count

64
00:07:04.819 --> 00:07:14.865
about Mina and my wedding plans. One particularly dark evening, I was shaving by the light of a

65
00:07:14.866 --> 00:07:24.492
candle lamp, using a hand mirror that Mina had given me the previous year as a birthday gift. Even

66
00:07:24.493 --> 00:07:28.436
though I did not see the count's reflection in the mirror, I suddenly felt his hand on my shoulder

67
00:07:28.437 --> 00:07:34.635
and jumped back in surprise, cutting my cheek with the razor. "Ouch!" I screamed and threw my hand

68
00:07:34.636 --> 00:07:37.524
over the cut. The count rushed toward me and pulled my hand away from my face, revealing a drop

69
00:07:37.525 --> 00:07:41.913
of blood. I saw a strange hunger in his eyes. Then, without warning, he grabbed the mirror and threw

70
00:07:41.914 --> 00:07:48.611
it on the floor. It broke into a thousand pieces, and without a word, he turned around and

71
00:07:48.612 --> 00:07:51.303
abruptly left the room. I heard him lock the door behind him. My heart was pounding, but it wasn't

72
00:07:51.304 --> 00:08:00.294
until I sat down on the bed to think about what had just happened that it dawned on

73
00:08:00.295 --> 00:08:04.849
me—I was a prisoner here! I was being held captive in Castle Dracula and there was no way out!

